description: Language policy — chat Russian, code English, docs Russian except README
alwaysApply: true
---

# Language

- **Chat:** Russian, unless the user asks otherwise.
- **Source code:** identifiers and comments in English (`src/`, `tools/`, CMake). Names of variables, functions, and classes are English.
- **Docs:** Russian. Exception: `README.md` is English. Do not translate existing Russian docs into English unless asked.
- **Git commits:** subject and body in English (imperative, why over what), even when chat is in Russian.
- **No Cursor attribution:** do not add `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>`, `Signed-off-by: Cursor`, `--trailer`, or set author/committer to the agent. The commit author is the person who asked for the commit.

```
# Chat / docs — Russian
Добавь правило про язык коммитов.

# Code comment — English
// Bind launch params, then pull only the requested outputs.

# Commit — English
Write git commit messages in English so history stays consistent.
```

`.pgg` comments follow the surrounding file (art examples in `resources/pgg` are Russian).
